Griptape follow-up: amend the commit message and also harden the griptape harness and regenerate all griptape extensions on your existing branch.

Decisions from the user: no follow-up PRs. Keep it all in this one griptape-focused PR; touching many extensions at once is fine.

Do:
1. Amend the commit message so the spec additions read as "observed against a cached copy of the previous spec", not as established fact.
2. Audit scripts/griptape-codegen for the same classes of bug the sibling harnesses (datadog, falai, snyk) turned up, and fix every one that applies, with tests:
   - shared fetch helper throwing on an empty 2xx body (202/204);
   - malformed JSON giving a bare SyntaxError without status/path;
   - no request timeout (use AbortSignal.timeout, with a clear error);
   - paginated helpers that assume a body;
   - response schemas with closed enums or required fields that would fail a whole page on one unexpected value (relax response side, keep request side strict);
   - generated tests that only assertExists instead of exercising execute and asserting request shape, and tests keyed so one method displaces another;
   - enum query args not asserted in the request URL;
   - descriptions truncated mid-word;
   - a change/version check that looks only at the model source and so misses helper or test changes.
   Sibling harnesses live in scripts/datadog-codegen, scripts/falai-codegen and scripts/snyk-codegen on their branches (worktrees under .claude/worktrees/agent-aac4e7dc2b9e04029, agent-a331cd7e22c35d83c, agent-ae0cf842eb579b6b8); read them for reference only, do not edit them.
3. Regenerate every griptape extension that changes. Each needs a CalVer bump, a RELEASE_NOTES.md written from the actual diff (state plainly when behavior is unchanged apart from hardening), and an appended identity upgrade entry.
4. Rerun all gates for the harness and every changed extension: check, lint, fmt:check, test, and `swamp extension quality manifest.yaml` (100%/passed).
5. Run pre-push-review again with its separate adversarial subagent (no self-review) until PASS. Fixes go in the harness, never in generated files.
6. Still STOP before pushing. Report as before, with an updated PR title and body covering the whole scope (re-pin plus hardening).

